# Ignore EVERYTHING in this directory by default (cleanliness audit 2026-11-13 #27). It used to
# ignore five prefixes, so ~900 run logs (every rig run, A/B chain and probe) showed as untracked and
# buried any real new source file in `git status`.
#
# A log worth keeping is a run record: commit it deliberately with `git add -f logs/<name>` and cite it
# from the report that uses it. Files already tracked here stay tracked (an ignore rule does not
# untrack); the ones nothing cites can be dropped with `git rm --cached`, which needs the owner's
# approval because the repo is public.
*
!.gitignore
